  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Carlos Rod\u00f3n lasted 3.2 innings. The offense got nothing when runners were on.",
    "what_this_means": "The bullpen hemorrhaged runs before the game was decided. They led after two innings, fell behind in the third, and couldn't climb back. Seventeen plate appearances with runners in scoring position. Three converted. The math doesn't work. Not against anyone, not in a division race. Jake Bird gave up an earned run in two-thirds of an inning. Brent Headrick's 1.2 were clean, but by then the damage was done. This game wasn't about the bullpen holding. It was about Rod\u00f3n exiting early and the lineup failing the one test that mattered. They had the moment. They didn't finish it.",
